      "side": 1,
      "message": "your method is n^2, for every item you traverse the list, up to the last item where you go n deep starting from 1... (assuming all startMs are not null) (if null it\u0027s plain n+n+n+n...)\n\nwe can use a slice that is a view of the original list instead, so no memory or real \"processing\" is done\n\nsortedLines.slice(index + 1 until sortedLines.size)\nThis is O(n) as for each item you search in its \u003eneighbourhood with worst case O(n-index) in case of null, but it should be close to never (and would be n+n-1+...+1)",
